{:edb/db-before-t 1289 :edb/db-after-t 1290 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534602 50 #inst "2026-10-12T04:25:04.841Z" 13194139534602 17592186045417 true] [17592186161716 1074 "We have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2}{5}\n$$\n\non the left and\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{6}{20}\n$$\n\non the right.\n\n![](images/f0/f087c076a86b5bab709af23db87d63ed66363d4d580c23dc453573f264fb28bc.png)\n\nTherefore, the multiplication problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2}{5} \\times \\dfrac{3}{4} = \\dfrac{6}{20}\n$$" 13194139534602 17592186045417 false] [17592186161716 1074 "We have $\\dfrac{2}{5}$ on the left and $\\dfrac{6}{20}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/f0/f087c076a86b5bab709af23db87d63ed66363d4d580c23dc453573f264fb28bc.png)\n\nTherefore, the multiplication problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2}{5} \\times \\dfrac{3}{4} = \\dfrac{6}{20}\n$$" 13194139534602 17592186045417 true] [17592186161717 1074 "We have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{4}\n$$\n\non the left and\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{9}{20}\n$$\n\non the right.\n\n![](images/31/31badccda3cc3548e2bdc40158e88d32feddcf92b8fdd4d4ae18f08396ca8cfc.png)\n\nThe shape on the right-hand side is split into $5$ equal parts by horizontal lines.\nSo, the shaded part on the right is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\color{blue}3}{5}\n$$\n\nof the shaded part on the left.\n\nTherefore, the multiplication problem shown is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{4} \\times \\dfrac{\\color{blue}3}{5} = \\dfrac{9}{20}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $\\color{blue}3$." 13194139534602 17592186045417 false] [17592186161717 1074 "We have $\\dfrac{3}{4}$ on the left and $\\dfrac{9}{20}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/31/31badccda3cc3548e2bdc40158e88d32feddcf92b8fdd4d4ae18f08396ca8cfc.png)\n\nThe shape on the right-hand side is split into $5$ equal parts by horizontal lines.\nSo, the shaded part on the right is $\\dfrac{\\color{blue}3}{5}$ of the shaded part on the left. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication problem shown is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{4} \\times \\dfrac{\\color{blue}3}{5} = \\dfrac{9}{20}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $\\color{blue}3.$" 13194139534602 17592186045417 true] [17592186161718 1074 "In the model, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2}{3}\n$$\n\non the left.\n\nSince we need to multiply by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\color{red}4}{\\color{blue}5}\n$$\n\n, we split the whole into $\\color{blue}5$ equal parts horizontally and ensure that $\\color{red}4$ of the parts remain shaded.\n\n![](images/97/978789f7aed1ea0e0dc8794aaeb00a3829168101e792129e72c0585fac43ebe2.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we see that the shaded part represents\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{8}{15}\n$$\n\nof the whole.\n\nTherefore, the missing picture is as follows:\n\n![](images/fa/faf527aba9974aa23b9a5bffd8fc8f54a2135fce10bf2d09a7133556ab4b95e3.png)" 13194139534602 17592186045417 false] [17592186161718 1074 "In the model, we have $\\dfrac{2}{3}$ on the left.\n\nSince we need to multiply by $\\dfrac{\\color{red}4}{\\color{blue}5}$, we split the whole into $\\color{blue}5$ equal parts horizontally and ensure that $\\color{red}4$ of the parts remain shaded.\n\n![](images/97/978789f7aed1ea0e0dc8794aaeb00a3829168101e792129e72c0585fac43ebe2.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we see that the shaded part represents $\\dfrac{8}{15}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore, the missing picture is as follows:\n\n![](images/fa/faf527aba9974aa23b9a5bffd8fc8f54a2135fce10bf2d09a7133556ab4b95e3.png)" 13194139534602 17592186045417 true] [17592186161719 1071 "![](images/60/6026c90a1101bf484ab649dcb35964ae4b136fc7784e384d1cf5d90ea47a96a2.png)\n\nUse the model above to calculate $\\dfrac{2}{6} \\times \\dfrac{3}{4}$." 13194139534602 17592186045417 false] [17592186161719 1071 "![](images/60/6026c90a1101bf484ab649dcb35964ae4b136fc7784e384d1cf5d90ea47a96a2.png)\n\nUse the model above to calculate $\\dfrac{2}{6} \\times \\dfrac{3}{4}.$" 13194139534602 17592186045417 true] [17592186161719 1074 "Since we need to multiply by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\color{red}3}{\\color{blue}4}\n$$\n\n, we split the whole into $\\color{blue}4$ equal parts horizontally and ensure that $\\color{red}3$ of the parts remain s