r\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\">$=$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" height=\"100\" rules=\"all\" width=\"100\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" 13194139534602 17592186045417 true] [17592186427477 1072 #uuid "077086cd-6950-5cf9-9941-247f49a033f6" 13194139534602 17592186045417 true] [17592186427477 1074 "We have $\\frac{2}{6}$ on the left and $\\frac{6}{24}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/91/918db9e617e1830739d91a5799f7862a56f988f9b5dc6ead60f1cdc41d332867.png)\n\nThe shape on the right-hand side is split into $4$ equal parts by horizontal lines.\nSo, the shaded part on the right is $\\frac{3}{4}$ of the shaded part on the left. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication problem shown is\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{6}\\times \\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{6}{24}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $3.$" 13194139534602 17592186045417 true] [17592186427478 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427474 13194139534602 17592186045417 true] [17592186427478 1069 "q-92177" 13194139534602 17592186045417 true] [17592186427478 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534602 17592186045417 true] [17592186427478 1071 "![](images/2a/2a373a3e79a3a225cb2c800a372337913c47ef3c3a78eae3305a137b4f4e7b3e.png)\n\nWhat multiplication problem is represented by the model above?" 13194139534602 17592186045417 true] [17592186427478 1072 #uuid "29d96c1a-468a-51d2-98aa-0f7dc0a4e8a2" 13194139534602 17592186045417 true] [17592186427478 1074 "We have $\\frac{2}{3}$ on the left and $\\frac{6}{15}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/41/4134d4b828fd388d27a028fd0bd90cd6fb04f0cb14b8fd3f43da148171773ddc.png)\n\nTherefore, the multiplication problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}\\times \\frac{3}{5}=\\frac{6}{15}\n$$" 13194139534602 17592186045417 true] [17592186427479 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427468 13194139534602 17592186045417 true] [17592186427479 1069 "q-92195" 13194139534602 17592186045417 true] [17592186427479 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534602 17592186045417 true] [17592186427479 1071 "![](images/71/71d2401577f8571e4abc2332183836c4e3c037bea74fba4021a8825e600f1ab2.png)\n\nWhat picture is missing from the multiplication model above?" 13194139534602 17592186045417 true] [17592186427479 1072 #uuid "3670d807-18c1-5863-9538-ea1e1c221139" 13194139534602 17592186045417 true] [17592186427479 1074 "In the model, we have $\\frac{3}{4}$ on the left.\n\nSince we need to multiply by $\\frac{4}{5}$, we split the whole into $5$ equal parts horizontally and ensure that $4$ of the parts remain shaded.\n\n![](images/b4/b40e2ec88f84324a67fed2df4726425e42971ba87c64714ba6521659d078495e.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\frac{12}{20}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore, the missing picture is as follows:\n\n![](images/bc/bcfd098d20bdaeaf4aaef601bf185f38bcfedec713e23b82d726bba8d08e75ea.png)" 13194139534602 17592186045417 true] [17592186427480 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427461 13194139534602 17592186045417 true] [17592186427480 1069 "q-60311" 13194139534602 17592186045417 true] [17592186427480 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534602 17592186045417 true] [17592186427480 1071 "![](images/a8/a817636d0f243a14eac09fe175beba71d0a1311c86ec86808600ed31ab49622d.png)\n\nWhat picture is missing from the multiplication model above?" 13194139534602 17592186045417 true] [17592186427480 1072 #uuid "38177e16-9481-59a0-81e0-6e58dd2d54cc" 13194139534602 17592186045417 true] [17592186427480 1074 "In the model, we have $\\frac{2}{5}$ on the left.\n\nSince we need to multiply by $\\frac{3}{4}$, we split the whole into $4$ equal parts horizontally and ensure that $3$ o